  "abstract": "Covers Package URL (purl) as standardized in ECMA-427 1st Edition (December 2025): the seven components, permitted and separator characters, per-component percent-encoding and case rules, the parse and build algorithms, lenient parsing and the purl-spec test suite, the PURL type definition schema and the registered types at purl-spec 1.0.1 and later with their normalizations, and the recommended qualifiers. It also covers the separately versioned VERS 1.2 version range specifier. Version lines: ECMA-427 1st Edition is current, the ECMA-427 2nd Edition draft is a preview with posture track, the pre-ECMA purl-spec text is legacy with an upgrade checklist, and VERS 1.2 is current in its own family. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions, syntax and encoding, parsing and building, types and qualifiers, and VERS.",
